    **Returning indices**

    If you set ``return_index=True``, then ``unique`` returns the indices of the
    first occurrence of each unique value:

    >>> x = jnp.array([3, 4, 1, 3, 1])
    >>> values, indices = jnp.unique(x, return_index=True)
    >>> print(values)
    [1 3 4]
    >>> print(indices)
    [2 0 1]
    >>> jnp.all(values == x[indices])
