    unique values for every entry in the input array:

    >>> x = jnp.array([3, 4, 1, 3, 1])
    >>> values, inverse = jnp.unique(x, return_inverse=True)
    >>> print(values)
    [1 3 4]
    >>> print(inverse)
    [1 2 0 1 0]
    >>> jnp.all(values[inverse] == x)
    Array(True, dtype=bool)

